---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { ABOUT_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`About ${SITE_TITLE} | Independent Creative Studio`}
			description={ABOUT_DESCRIPTION}
		/>
	</head>
	<body class="about-page">
		<a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>
		<SiteHeader />
		<main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
			<header class="about-page__intro">
				<p class="eyebrow">About Petalwake</p>
				<h1>Stories matter<br /><em>because people do.</em></h1>
				<p class="about-page__lead">
					Petalwake Studios is an independent creative studio exploring the beauty, complexity,
					and wonder of the human experience through film, animation, and original media.
				</p>
				<p>
					We create stories inspired by the things that shape us: love, loss, memory, forgiveness,
					hope, and the quiet moments that give life meaning. Through cinematic imagery, atmosphere,
					music, and visual storytelling, we seek to make work that lingers beyond the screen.
				</p>
			</header>

			<section class="about-page__section" aria-labelledby="why-stories-title">
				<p class="eyebrow">Why stories</p>
				<div>
					<h2 id="why-stories-title">A life beyond our own</h2>
					<p>
						A story can take us somewhere we have never been and place us inside a life we have
						never lived. For a while, we see the world from another person’s side of the door.
						That encounter can complicate what we assumed and make room for a more honest kind
						of compassion.
					</p>
					<p>
						We begin with people and the choices they make, not with a lesson to deliver. The
						questions matter because the lives around them matter.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="about-page__section about-page__section--light" aria-labelledby="wonder-title">
				<p class="eyebrow">Stories that awaken wonder</p>
				<div>
					<h2 id="wonder-title">More than spectacle</h2>
					<p>
						Wonder can live in a landscape, but it can also appear in an ordinary kindness, a
						difficult truth finally spoken, or the possibility of beginning again. It is the
						surprise of finding beauty in a world that also holds suffering—and of discovering
						that a person is more than their worst moment.
					</p>
					<p>
						We want to stay attentive to the mystery and beauty of being alive, without looking
						away from what makes life difficult.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="about-page__section" aria-labelledby="questions-title">
				<p class="eyebrow">A place for questions</p>
				<div>
					<h2 id="questions-title">Room to reflect</h2>
					<p>
						We are drawn to stories that look directly at grief, guilt, responsibility, and
						forgiveness without pretending that any of them are simple. People can be wounded
						and still answer for the harm they cause. Reconciliation may be possible, but it
						cannot be demanded or assumed.
					</p>
					<p>
						We do not ask every viewer to reach the same conclusion. Our hope is to create space
						for reflection, conversation, connection, and, sometimes, healing.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="about-page__section about-page__section--closing" aria-labelledby="looking-forward-title">
				<p class="eyebrow">Looking forward</p>
				<div>
					<h2 id="looking-forward-title">One story at a time</h2>
					<p>
						Petalwake is an independent creative studio growing toward a larger vision. We are
						building that future carefully, beginning with the work in front of us and leaving
						room for the stories still to come. Whatever their form, we want them to begin with
						people and stay open to wonder.
					</p>
					<p><a href="/#work">Explore Petalwake Films <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>
		<SiteFooter />
	</body>
</html>
